{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":487912,"name":"Sinn","username":"Sinn","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/s/a9adbd/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-10T07:09:06.674Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eI’m a Cursor Pro user and I have a question about the Included Usage breakdown.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/d/2/d2944a58fb87703ce583471ccb1b952f94070284.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/u2RYJpfKaE0NyglbqLv3yEWkAgk.png?dl=1\" title=\"iShot_2026-09-10_15.05.08\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/d/2/d2944a58fb87703ce583471ccb1b952f94070284_2_690x264.png\" alt=\"iShot_2026-09-10_15.05.08\" data-base62-sha1=\"u2RYJpfKaE0NyglbqLv3yEWkAgk\" width=\"690\" height=\"264\" srcset=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/d/2/d2944a58fb87703ce583471ccb1b952f94070284_2_690x264.png, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/d/2/d2944a58fb87703ce583471ccb1b952f94070284_2_1035x396.png 1.5x, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/d/2/d2944a58fb87703ce583471ccb1b952f94070284_2_1380x528.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"F7F7F7\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003eiShot_2026-09-10_15.05.08\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e2246×860 72.5 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAs shown in the screenshot, my Cursor Models usage is currently 23.1%, but a large portion comes from Grok Bot related usage:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003egrok-bot-default: 10.0%\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003egrok-bot-automation: 3.9%\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTogether, Grok Bot usage accounts for around 14% of my Cursor Models usage.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI thought Grok Bot had its own weekly included usage pool separate from the monthly Cursor Models quota.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCould you please clarify:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAre grok-bot-default and grok-bot-automation actually counted against my monthly Cursor Models quota?\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIf not, why are they displayed under Cursor Models in Included Usage?\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWill Grok Bot usage affect my remaining quota for Composer / Cursor Grok models?\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThanks!\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-10T07:30:27.157Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":22,"reads":10,"readers_count":9,"score":122.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":171226,"topic_slug":"why-is-grok-bot-usage-included-in-my-cursor-models-usage","display_username":"Sinn","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":3,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":137115,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/why-is-grok-bot-usage-included-in-my-cursor-models-usage/171226/1","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":true,"can_vote":false},{"id":487920,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-10T07:30:02.468Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, thanks for the detailed write-up and the screenshot. On your three questions:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo. \u003ccode\u003egrok-bot-default\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003egrok-bot-automation\u003c/code\u003e don’t count against your monthly Cursor Models quota. Grok Bot chats and automations are metered against Grok Bot’s own weekly allowance, which isn’t tied to your Cursor plan. The only exception is cloud coding agents that Grok Bot runs for you. Those count against your Cursor plan like any other cloud agent. You don’t have any of those runs.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThey show up there because of a display issue we’re already tracking. The per-model breakdown under Cursor Models isn’t filtering out Grok Bot rows yet, so they appear in the list and take up part of the percentage. The 23.1% header is correct and reflects only your real usage in the Cursor app. Only the rows under it are labelled wrong.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo. Grok Bot usage won’t reduce your remaining Composer or Cursor Grok model quota. The only way Grok Bot touches your Cursor plan is via the cloud agent case in point 1.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNothing needs fixing on your account. Once the breakdown is corrected, the grok-bot rows will disappear from that list, and your own Cursor model percentages will increase up to the same 23.1% (the header will stay the same). I’ll reply here if there’s an update.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":4,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-10T07:30:02.468Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":9,"readers_count":8,"score":36.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":171226,"topic_slug":"why-is-grok-bot-usage-included-in-my-cursor-models-usage","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":2}],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":750,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/why-is-grok-bot-usage-included-in-my-cursor-models-usage/171226/4","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":2}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":2,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":true,"topic_accepted_answer":true},{"id":487935,"name":"Sinn","username":"Sinn","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/s/a9adbd/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-10T07:50:31.523Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThanks for the detailed explanation, Dean. This clears up my confusion about the Grok Bot usage display issue.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBy the way, I’m a new Cursor user and I’ve been really enjoying Composer 2.5. It has become my preferred model for daily coding because of its speed and coding performance.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI was wondering if there are plans to continue evolving the Composer model line. Composer 2.5 has been available for several months now, and I’m curious whether a future Composer version is currently being developed.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI understand you may not be able to share specific release dates, but I’d love to know whether Composer is still an active focus for the team.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThanks again!\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":7,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-10T07:50:31.523Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":4,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":9,"readers_count":8,"score":1.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":171226,"topic_slug":"why-is-grok-bot-usage-included-in-my-cursor-models-usage","display_username":"Sinn","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"reply_to_user":{"id":750,"username":"deanrie","name":"Dean Rie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":137115,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/why-is-grok-bot-usage-included-in-my-cursor-models-usage/171226/7","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":true}],"stream":[487912,487920,487935]},"timeline_lookup":[[1,1]],"suggested_topics":[],"tags":[{"id":416,"name":"grok-bot","slug":"grok-bot"}],"tags_descriptions":{},"fancy_title":"Why is Grok Bot usage included in my Cursor Models usage?","id":171226,"title":"Why is Grok Bot usage included in my Cursor Models usage?","posts_count":3,"created_at":"2026-09-10T07:09:06.624Z","views":51,"reply_count":1,"like_count":3,"last_posted_at":"2026-09-10T07:50:31.523Z","visible":true,"closed":false,"archived":false,"has_summary":false,"archetype":"regular","slug":"why-is-gro