 Bot is using my first-party / Cursor Models allowance","id":170742,"title":"Cursor Team: Grok Bot is using my first-party / Cursor Models allowance","slug":"cursor-team-grok-bot-is-using-my-first-party-cursor-models-allowance","posts_count":5,"reply_count":2,"highest_post_number":10,"image_url":null,"created_at":"2026-09-06T01:25:38.763Z","last_posted_at":"2026-09-07T16:18:08.398Z","bumped":true,"bumped_at":"2026-09-07T16:18:08.398Z","archetype":"regular","unseen":false,"pinned":false,"unpinned":null,"excerpt":"I’m on Cursor Teams. \nGrok Bot usage is showing up under the first-party (Cursor Models) allowance on my seat(Cursor Team), and it is increasing that percentage. \nOn Pro, staff said Grok Bot has its own weekly pool and s\u0026hellip;","visible":true,"closed":false,"archived":false,"bookmarked":null,"liked":null,"thumbnails":null,"tags":[{"id":416,"name":"grok-bot","slug":"grok-bot"}],"tags_descriptions":{},"like_count":0,"views":91,"category_id":8,"featured_link":null,"op_like_count":0,"has_accepted_answer":false,"posters":[{"extras":null,"description":"Original Poster","user":{"id":129603,"username":"harrisonhou","name":"harrisonhou","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/h/cdc98d/{size}.png","trust_level":1}},{"extras":null,"description":"Recent Poster","user":{"id":103596,"username":"mohitjain","name":"Mohit","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/mohitjain/{size}/100229_2.png","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_group_id":42,"primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","admin":true,"moderator":true,"trust_level":4}},{"extras":"latest","description":"Most Recent Poster","user":{"id":19170,"username":"TByte007","name":"Iasen Kostov","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/tbyte007/{size}/19342_2.png","trust_level":2}}]},{"fancy_title":"Cloud Environment Setip","id":170420,"title":"Cloud Environment Setip","slug":"cloud-environment-setip","posts_count":3,"reply_count":1,"highest_post_number":7,"image_url":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T04:57:50.587Z","last_posted_at":"2026-09-10T01:25:25.511Z","bumped":true,"bumped_at":"2026-09-10T01:25:25.511Z","archetype":"regular","unseen":false,"pinned":false,"unpinned":null,"excerpt":"Where does the bug appear (feature/product)?\nCursor IDE \nDescribe the Bug\nFollowing this post: \n\nIt appears that cloud environment setup: \n\nstill uses Opus 4.8\nstill fails to give any indication, warning, or otherwise sh\u0026hellip;","visible":true,"closed":false,"archived":false,"bookmarked":null,"liked":null,"thumbnails":null,"tags":[{"id":312,"name":"cloud-agents","slug":"cloud-agents"},{"id":340,"name":"anthropic","slug":"anthropic"},{"id":341,"name":"grok","slug":"grok"}],"tags_descriptions":{},"like_count":0,"views":60,"category_id":6,"featured_link":null,"op_like_count":0,"has_accepted_answer":false,"posters":[{"extras":"latest","description":"Original Poster, Most Recent Poster","user":{"id":135244,"username":"jnotts","name":"","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/j/b4bc9f/{size}.png","trust_level":0}},{"extras":null,"description":"Recent Poster","user":{"id":105146,"username":"kevinn","name":"Kevin Neilson","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/kevinn/{size}/101206_2.png","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_group_id":42,"primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","admin":true,"moderator":true,"trust_level":3}}]}],"summarizable":false,"has_cached_summary":false,"valid_reactions":["heart","+1","crossed_fingers","clap","laughing","open_mouth","confetti_ball","hugs","heavy_plus_sign","heart_eyes","sunglasses","cursor"],"accepted_answers":[{"id":487920,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-10T07:30:02.468Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, thanks for the detailed write-up and the screenshot. On your three questions:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo. \u003ccode\u003egrok-bot-default\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003egrok-bot-automation\u003c/code\u003e don’t count against your monthly Cursor Models quota. Grok Bot chats and automations are metered against Grok Bot’s own weekly allowance, which isn’t tied to your Cursor plan. The only exception is cloud coding agents that Grok Bot runs for you. Those count against your Cursor plan like any other cloud agent. You don’t have any of those runs.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThey show up there because of a display issue we’re already tracking. The per-model breakdown under Cursor Models isn’t filtering out Grok Bot rows yet, so they appear in the list and take up part of the percentage. The 23.1% header is correct and reflects only your real usage in the Cursor app. Only the rows under it are labelled wrong.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo. Grok Bot usage won’t reduce your remaining Composer or Cursor Grok model quota. The only way Grok Bot touches your Cursor plan is via the cloud agent case in point 1.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNothing needs fixing on your account. Once the breakdown is corrected, the grok-bot rows will disappear from that list, and your own Cursor model percentages will increase up to the same 23.1% (the header will stay the same). I’ll reply here if there’s an update.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":4,"topic_id":171226,"url":"/t/why-is-grok-bot-usage-included-in-my-cursor-models-usage/171226/4","accepter_name":"Sinn","accepter_username":"Sinn"}],"has_accepted_answer":true,"can_create_shared_issue":false,"shared_issue_visible":false,"can_vote":false,"vote_count":0,"user_voted":false,"discourse_zendesk_plugin_zendesk_id":null,"discourse_zendesk_plugin_zendesk_url":"https://your-url.zendesk.com/agent/tickets/","details":{"can_edit":false,"notification_level":1,"participants":[{"id":137115,"username":"Sinn","name":"Sinn","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/s/a9adbd/{size}.png","post_count":2,"primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"trust_level":0},{"id":750,"username":"deanrie","name":"Dean Rie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","post_count":1,"primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_color":"","flair_bg_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"admin":true,"moderator":true,"trust_level":4}],"created_by":{"id":137115,"username":"Sinn","name":"Sinn","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/s/a9adbd/{size}.png"},"last_poster":{"id":137115,"username":"Sinn","name":"Sinn","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/s/a9adbd/{size}.png"}},"bookmarks":[]}